title: The Spring Soviet Elections
face-image: img/events/spring_elections.jpg
subtitle: The provincial capitals vote.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: dix >= 30 and bol_regime = 1
priority: 30
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
var extra = {men: 1.0 + 0.004 * Q.soviet_democracy, sr: 1.0 + 0.003 * Q.soviet_democracy, bol: 1.0 + Q.repression / 150};
RO.setResults(Q, 'provincial', extra, 100);
RO.recordParliament(Q, 'spring', 'The spring soviet elections: share of the vote');
Q.opp_share = Q.res_men + Q.res_sr + Q.res_lsr + Q.res_oth * 0.5;
Q.capitals_won = Math.round(30 * RO.clamp((Q.opp_share - 30) / 32, 0, 1));
Q.spring_honoured = 0;
Q.poll_men_d = Math.round(Q.res_men);
!}

= The Spring Soviet Elections

During the spring of 1918, soviets across Russia held new elections. The Bolsheviks had expected to win everywhere. In the cities where the Soviet government had been recognised, the opposition (the Mensheviks, the SRs and their allies) won majorities in [+ capitals_won +] of the 30 provincial capitals where elections were held. In the second half of the spring, the new soviets were dispersed by force, on the ground that the "mood of the masses had been misread".

By our count, the vote was:

{!<div class="parliament" data-name="spring"></div>!}

- @protest: Accept the annulment, and protest.
- @renounce: Offer to renounce armed struggle in return for the results being honoured.

@protest
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {soviet_democracy: -3, repression: 2, rel_bol: -3});
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 3, railway: 2});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 1, -2);
if (Q.capitals_won >= 19) { Q.spring_won = 1; }
!}

The results were annulled in town after town. Menshevik delegates were turned out of the soviets and their newspapers closed. We protested, and published the results.

@renounce
on-arrival: {!
Q.renounced_armed = 1;
Q.honour_ok = (Q.soviet_democracy >= 50 - 4 * Q.bloc_lean && Q.rel_bol >= 30 && Q.capitals_won >= 10) ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.honour_ok) {
    Q.spring_honoured = 1;
    RO.add(Q, {soviet_democracy: 5, repression: -3, rel_bol: 4});
    RO.boost(Q, {workers: 4, railway: 3});
} else {
    RO.add(Q, {soviet_democracy: -2, rel_bol: -2});
    RO.boost(Q, {workers: 1});
}
if (Q.capitals_won >= 19) { Q.spring_won = 1; }
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 8);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 1, -3);
!}
go-to: spring_deal if honour_ok = 1; spring_no_deal if honour_ok = 0

@spring_deal

The Central Executive Committee has agreed, under pressure from the Left SRs and a section of the Bolsheviks, to honour most of the results in return for a pledge from the opposition parties that they would not take up arms against the government. Many soviets have been allowed to continue.

@spring_no_deal

The Bolsheviks listened politely, and said that the soviets would be dissolved anyway. The pledge has been given, and, for the time being, it is worth nothing.
